# Quotes

Prefer **single quotes** over double quotes in TypeScript/JavaScript and JSX.

Matches `.prettierrc`: `singleQuote: true`, `jsxSingleQuote: true`.

```tsx
// ❌
import { Ri } from "@/Icons";
<div data-slot="details" className="kicl-color-grey-dark" />
querySelector('[data-slot="select-trigger"]');

// ✅
import { Ri } from '@/Icons';
<div data-slot='details' className='kicl-color-grey-dark' />
querySelector(`[data-slot='select-trigger']`);
```

When a string needs nested quotes (selectors, documented attrs), prefer a **template literal** with single quotes inside - not a single-quoted string wrapping double quotes. Same in JSDoc: `` `is='a'` ``, `` `role='none'` ``.

Exceptions: JSON, strings that contain apostrophes where escaping would hurt readability, and generated/vendor files.
